# Day 22

**21km / 5.5 hours**

![Just when I thought I was done, the beach pulls me back in](./beach.jpg)

The day began with a gentle enough road walk for a few kilometres before revealing its true intentions as the beach unfurled. With 3 bodies of water to cross and a long beach it wouldn't be an easy day ahead.

Each stream/estuary to cross was vastly different depending on the tide at the time and my timing was poor such that I ended up having to cross a few of them near to high tide. With the final estuary I tried to cross a bit higher up, not realising that it was deeper and fast-moving up there so I had to backtrack and find a nicer spot to get past.

![A cool dotterel I saw along the way.](./dotterel.jpg)

![A cool tern I saw along the way, not the super rare one though.](./tern.jpg)

I also saw a few cool birds, there are some rare fairy terns but I didn't find any of them.